> Sch[warz] has been the president of the Greater Cleveland Film Commission for over ten years. He has over thirty years of[ experience] in the film and television industries, working predominantly as a location manager and producer.[ His work] includes “[Wild] At Heart,” “My Name Is Earl,” “Entourage,” “The[ Come]back,” “From[ the] Earth to the Moon” and Tom Hanks and Steven Spielberg’s “Band of Brothers,” for which Ivan won a Golden Globe.
The Film Commission is the only nonprofit organization dedicated to bringing jobs and economic impact to Northeast Ohio through the growth of a sustainable media production industry. Since passing the Ohio Motion Picture Tax Credit in 2009, more than 110 productions have shot in Cleveland, including “The Avengers,” “Captain America: The Winter Soldier,” and most recently, Matthew McCon[aug]hey’s �[�White Boy] Rick” and Helen Hunt’s “I See You”.


